        "Nilkamal sofas predominantly use fabric upholstery -- a practical choice that wears differently from leatherette. Fabric upholstery does not peel the way synthetic leather does, but it does pill, fade, fray, and tear over time. High-contact areas like armrests, seat cushion edges, and headrests typically show wear first. Staining is also common, particularly on lighter-coloured fabrics.",
        "FurniRevive's fabric upholstery repair services cover everything from small tear repairs and patch work to full re-upholstery. For minor damage, we use matching fabric patches and professional upholstery adhesives and stitching to repair the affected area invisibly where possible. For more extensive wear affecting large areas of the sofa, full re-upholstery is the most practical solution -- it restores the sofa completely and allows you to choose a new fabric that may be more durable or better suited to your home. Upholstery pricing starts at Rs.3000 per seat for fabric and Rs.4000 per seat for leatherette.",
