        "The most common Nilkamal office chair repair is pneumatic cylinder (gas lift) replacement. The pneumatic cylinder is the pressurised gas spring that allows the chair height to be adjusted. Over time, the seal in the cylinder wears out and the chair begins to slowly sink to its lowest position when weight is applied. Replacing the cylinder -- typically a 30-60 minute job -- fully restores the height adjustment function. We carry standard cylinder sizes compatible with most Nilkamal office chair models. Tilt mechanism repairs restore the backrest tilt and tilt lock functions. Armrest repairs address loose, broken, or detached armrests. Base and wheel replacement is available for cracked plastic bases or worn-out caster wheels.",
